# Build artefacts
out/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Only `data/vault.sqlite` -- the real snapshot -- is committed. See
# .github/workflows/index.yml for why it is committed at all: a cache would be
# evicted, and a snapshot that vanishes has to be rebuilt from the deployment block,
# which is slow and on some public endpoints not permitted.
#
# It is the BASE SEPOLIA snapshot, and the workflow is the only thing that should write
# to it. A local run defaults to `data/vault-<chainId>.sqlite` instead -- here
# `data/vault-31337.sqlite` -- because when the default was this path, a local anvil run
# wrote 33,702 local blocks into the published snapshot beside a Base Sepolia
# deployment. The rows were ignored by this rule, not by the indexer.
#
# Everything else here is disposable: the write-ahead log and shared-memory file are
# transient, and a repository holding a WAL without its database is a corrupt database
# rather than a slightly stale one; scratch databases from tests and from developing
# by hand would be a second, conflicting copy of the index.
data/*.sqlite
data/*.sqlite-wal
data/*.sqlite-shm
data/*.sqlite-journal
!data/vault.sqlite

# Scratch output. Anything written into data/ that is not the snapshot is disposable,
# and a JSON file of a response captured while developing would be a second copy of
# data the API already serves.
data/*.json
data/_*

# Node
node_modules/

# Environment
.env
.env.*

# Editor and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
